WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.160
In many ways, the Russian invasion of Ukraine&nbsp;
felt all too familiar to the people of Taiwan.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:11.440
Here is a larger, more powerful,&nbsp;
authoritarian, and revisionist bully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.920
attacking its democratic neighbor for&nbsp;
nothing more than historical proximity.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:21.440
And beneath a mountain of explanations,&nbsp;
theories, and models is really just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:28.000
one man’s deranged pursuit of empire. Or,&nbsp;
something else entirely — we truly don’t know.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:36.320
It even began like we expect an attack on Taiwan&nbsp;
would — with a long, drawn-out buildup of forces,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.520
followed by a sudden and&nbsp;
chaotic barrage of missiles.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:45.200
With very large present populations&nbsp;
but below-replacement fertility,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:50.560
both China and Russia are what you might call&nbsp;
“demographies in decline” — and there isn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:58.640
much time left. A man born today can expect to&nbsp;
live 74 years in China and a mere 67 in Russia.
 &nbsp;

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:04.400
“Ukraine today, Taiwan tomorrow”&nbsp;
isn’t just hypothetical, either.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:10.800
Quote “reunifying” with the island has been the&nbsp;
goal of every Chinese leader for the last 70 years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:15.120
and chairman Xi Jinping has gone well&nbsp;
out of his way to eliminate ambiguity.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:20.320
Needless to say, China’s refusal to call&nbsp;
Russia’s actions in Ukraine what they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:25.840
are — an invasion — wasn’t too comforting&nbsp;
to the 23 million residents of Taiwan.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:33.680
…Yet, China is not Russia. And Taiwan is&nbsp;
not Ukraine. For all their similarities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.520
there remain huge differences the&nbsp;
world would be unwise to ignore.

